course: dictionary
lesson: 7172
title: Permission
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Permission means someone in charge says yes, and you are allowed to do something. «Play online only with people your family knows about, and with your parents' permission.» The words around permission tell you that a parent must say yes before you play.
explain: To ask permission means to ask if you may do something. «Picking flowers from someone's garden needs their permission first.» The word first is a clue: you ask before you pick, not after.
explain: Look at the little phrases around permission: with permission, without permission, give permission. «Never buy gems, coins or loot boxes in a game without a parent's permission» tells you that buying without a yes is not allowed.
explain: Permission is usually a word we do not count. You need permission, not a permission. When you read it, ask: who is in charge here, and did they say yes?
fact: Permission means being allowed to do something because someone in charge has said yes.
fact: To ask permission means to ask if you may do something.
fact: A permission slip is a form a parent signs to say a child can go on a trip.
fact: Body safety rule: nobody may touch you without your permission.
fact: In computing, permissions are settings that say who may open, change or use a file or app.
exercise: What does permission mean? | Asking someone a question about the time | A kind of sweet eaten at school | *Being allowed to do something, because someone in charge says yes | Being forced to do something you do not want
exercise: In «Picking flowers from someone's garden needs their permission first.», what must you get before you pick? | A picture of the flowers | *Their permission | A ladder | A bigger basket
exercise: A form that a parent signs so a child can go on a trip is called a what? | Parent letter | School bag | Trip ticket | *Permission slip
test: Which phrase means doing something when nobody has said yes? | With permission | Give permission | Ask permission | *Without permission
test: In «Never buy gems, coins or loot boxes in a game without a parent's permission», who must say yes before a child buys them? | The child's best friend | The shop assistant | The game company | *A parent
exam: Which sentence shows someone asking permission? | The house is at the end of the road | *Mum, may I go to Sam's house after school? | I went to Sam's house and forgot to tell anyone | Sam gave me a present for my birthday
